PURPOSE Price one physical vehicle path using the paper's Eq. 32 objective.
REFERENCES Paper Eqs. 32--36; SubProblemGeneratorVeh.cs.
ASSUMPTIONS Eq. 32 indexes duals by an existing vehicle route l. For a new route,
    pricingContext selects a reference route lRef owned by k; orchestration tests
    every such context. This reference-route convention is a design choice where
    the paper leaves indexing unspecified. Its result is scoped to that context,
    rather than a reduced-cost oracle for a fixed full master.
INPUT immutable network, vehicleId k, current master duals, inherited vehicle
    branches, pricingContext(lRef,rowSignature,poolSignature), solve limits.
OUTPUT VehiclePricingResult with candidate path, objective and bound for this
    context, solver status, physical cost, signatures and validation outcome.

PROCEDURE SolveSeparateVehicleModel(network,k,duals,vehicleBranches,pricingContext,limits)
    Require owner(lRef)=k, current dual/row/pool signatures and a complete catalog.
    Create binary y[k,i,t,j,t'] for each ordinary operating-path arc in A_e,k.
    The explicit vo->vd unused-vehicle connector is already represented by its
        seed route and is excluded from this operating-path pricing model.
    sourceFlow := net outflow over the complete virtual-source connector family.
    add sourceFlow=1 and net inflow over the complete sink connector family=1.
    FOR every internal vehicle state
        add total outgoing y - total incoming y = 0.
    add SUM_(i,t,j,t') duration[k,i,t,j,t']*y[k,i,t,j,t']
        <= sourceFlow*maximumDuty[k].
    Apply permitted vehicle type/zone, fixed service and committed-arc conditions
        represented by this epoch's catalog and inherited hard constraints.
    FOR every branch on vehicle k
        Resolve the full immutable arc key to its original record.
        For forbid: add y[record]=0. For force: add y[record]=1.
        If a forced record is absent: RETURN context_infeasible.
        If a key is ambiguous: RETURN branch_key_failure.

    pricingObjective := etaK * SUM_(i,t,j,t') c[k,i,t,j,t']*y[k,i,t,j,t'].
    FOR each vehicle arc (i,t,j,t') and order r
        Match the paper's complete endpoint/state transition to lRef's rows.
        pricingObjective += y[k,i,t,j,t'] *
            (-u^beta[lRef,r,i,t,j,t'] + u^alpha[lRef,r,i,t,j,t']).
    pricingObjective -= sourceFlow * u^epsilon[k].
    FOR each vehicle arc (i,t,j,t')
        pricingObjective -= y[k,i,t,j,t'] * capacity[k] *
                            u^cap[lRef,i,t,j,t'].
    Terms outside the defined supported-row domain are zero. A missing dual for
        an existing row is an error, not an implicit zero.
    Set objective, optimize within limits and store status/bound before extraction.
    IF no incumbent: RETURN no_candidate with solverStatus and context identity.
    Check binary residual; snap only within integralityTolerance.
    Extract and order the single k source-to-sink path, including idle if selected.
    Validate timing, flow, duty, epoch commitments and every inherited branch.
    Reject detached cycles; if the catalog is not acyclic, add explicit path/cycle
        constraints before solving.
    originalObjective := evaluate pricingObjective on the audited path.
    Require agreement with the solver incumbent objective within objectiveTolerance.
    physicalCost := SUM original arc costs; do not substitute pricing coefficients.
    RETURN VehiclePricingResult{vehicleId=k,referenceRouteId=lRef,candidate,
        pricingObjective=originalObjective,solverLowerBound,solverStatus,
        physicalCost,validation=passed,poolSignature,rowSignature,branchSignature}.

STATUS CONTRACT
    optimal_context means the entire declared operating-path model was solved for
        this one lRef. time_limit with a valid negative incumbent can add a route.
    A nonnegative incumbent under a time limit cannot establish exhaustion.
    Proven infeasibility exhausts this declared operating-path context; it is
        compatible with an owner represented only by an unused seed route.
    If a current admissible operating route exists for k yet this same-scope
        pricing model is infeasible, report a catalog/branch consistency problem.
    No-progress results identify both k and lRef and use the path of vehicle k.
